# Neo Learn Spectral parameters (docs/specs/neo-learn.md, neo-learn-controls.md A1 and A2.12). The order is permanent: songs and
# presets store values by position. The 12 controls are the six core ones, then the six global ones (Attack, Decay, Sustain, Release,
# Unison / Spread, Output). Each has a snake_case id, and the Explain text (How, Sound; the description is the How line).
# Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoLearnSpectral
namespace NeoBuzz.LearnSpectral
class NeoLearnSpectralMachine
tracks 16
summary Teaching spectral resynthesiser: one Dye Essence patch driven by 12 controls. One sample (Dye's five built-in ones, or your own WAV) is analysed once into its partials and its noise, then rebuilt at any key, speed and spacing: a stretch of the partials, a time smear, a freeze that holds one moment, a gate that keeps only the loudest partials and a balance between the tonal and noisy halves, with an ADSR, unison and an output gain. Every control says what it does and what you will hear. Use it for frozen pads, bell-like stretches, ghostly textures and slowed-down sounds, or to learn how analysis-resynthesis works.
import sample .wav | A WAV sample (mono or stereo, up to 20 s, kept in the machine state with its analysis): the sample the Source control's User choice plays

group Core
SpectralShift    "Stretch" 0 1000 500 bip
    id spectral_shift
    how Moves each partial away from its whole multiple of the pitch (+ spreads them apart, - bunches them), without changing the pitch of the note.
    sound Positive values turn the sample bell-like, metallic and glassy; negative values make it dense, thick and clustered; 0% is the sample as recorded.

SpectralBlur     "Time Smear" 0 1000 0 pct
    id spectral_blur
    how Averages the analysed partials over time (up to 300 ms either side), so that each moment of the sample drifts into its neighbours.
    sound Sharp attacks and movement smear into a liquid, washed-out blur; at 100% the sample is a slow cloud.

SpectralFreeze   "Freeze" 0 1000 0 pct
    id spectral_freeze
    how Slows the reading of the analysis to a stop and moves where it starts to 40% into the sample; at 100% one moment of the sample is held for as long as the key is down.
    sound Turns the sound into a held, steady tone made of one instant of the recording; part-way it is the sample slowed down with its pitch kept.

Source           "Source" 0 5 0 enum Choir Strings Bell Pluck Texture User
    id spectral_source
    how Selects the recording that is analysed and played across the keyboard: Dye Essence's `Choir`, `Strings`, `Bell`, `Pluck`, `Texture`, or `User`, a WAV you load.
    sound Changes the raw material every other control reshapes; each one has a different mix of partials and noise.

PartialGate      "Partial Gate" 0 1000 0 pct
    id bin_gate
    how Keeps only the loudest partials of the analysis: all 64 at 0%, a single one at 100%.
    sound Strips away the weaker overtones, leaving a thinner, whistling or sine-like core; the noise is not touched.

ToneNoise        "Tone / Noise" 0 1000 500 pct
    id tonal_noise
    how Balances the two halves of the analysis: 0% plays only the noise, 50% both as recorded, 100% only the partials.
    sound Left, the sample is a breathy, whispering wash with no pitch; right, a clean, pure, almost synthetic tone.

group Global
EnvAttack        "Attack" 0 1000 300 time 0.0005 5
    id env_attack
    how Sets the time required for the note's amplitude (and routed envelope modulation) to ramp from silence to full peak after a note-on trigger.
    sound Low values create immediate, percussive plucks; high values produce slow, swelling pads.
EnvDecay         "Decay" 0 1000 600 time 0.005 8
    id env_decay
    how Controls how long it takes for the signal to drop from peak level down to the sustain level while a key remains held.
    sound Short decay makes notes snappy and tight; longer decay gives a gradual piano- or bell-like fade.
EnvSustain       "Sustain" 0 1000 800 pct
    id env_sustain
    how Defines the steady-state volume level maintained for as long as a note is held after the Attack and Decay stages complete.
    sound At 0% the synth behaves like a plucked or struck instrument; at 100% it holds full organ-like volume.
EnvRelease       "Release" 0 1000 500 time 0.005 10
    id env_release
    how Sets the time required for the sound to fade from its current level to complete silence after the note is released.
    sound Short release stops notes abruptly; long release leaves an ambient tail that blends chords together.
UnisonDetune     "Unison / Spread" 0 1000 0 pct
    id unison_detune
    how 0% plays one voice per note; above 0% each note plays 5 detuned, stereo-spread voices (3 in Additive, Granular and Spectral), with detune (up to ±50 cents) and width growing with the value.
    sound Thickens thin waveforms into wide, chorus-like stereo leads and pads.
OutputGain       "Output" 0 1000 665 db -36 12
    id output_gain
    how Sets the level after synthesis. There is no limiter (NeoBuzz mixes in floating point); a clip light shows when the output passes 0 dBFS.
    sound Controls overall loudness; keep the clip light dark when the next machine expects levels at or below 0 dBFS.

# What the machine measures (NeoLearnSpectralMachine.Readings, machine_readings): the output after Output, in dBFS.
reading rms_db dB | The output's RMS over about half a second (-inf: silence)
reading peak_db dB | The output's peak, falling 20 dB a second (-inf: silence)
reading active_voices notes | Notes sounding now (unison voices belong to their note)
